{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-328474",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 1.96)=0.975.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\ge 1.96)=1-0.975=0.025.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-1.96)=0.025.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14165008/assets/e46e28a748745da14c260af2c39c7c10983b40476c57d8d75a51f0390d2359d2.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.96) & =0.025 \\\\ P(Z\\le -1.96) & =0.025.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required value of $z$ is $-1.96.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
